# Demo Project Structure

This document describes the structure of the demo project, which is a React-based web application built with Vite and TypeScript.

## Project Overview

The demo project is a modern web application that uses React 19, TypeScript, and Vite as its core technologies. It follows a modular architecture with clear separation of concerns.

## Source Code Structure (`src/`)

### Core Module (`core/`)
- `store/` - State management implementation and store configurations
- `repository/` - Data access layer and repository implementations (e.g., PaneRepository)
- `helper/` - Core utility functions and helper methods
- `constant/` - Application-wide constants and configuration values
- `entity/` - Core domain models and type definitions

### Design System (`design/`)
- `util/` - Design system utilities and helper functions
- `style/` - Global styles, themes, and design tokens
- `component/` - Reusable design system components
- `hook/` - Custom React hooks for design system functionality

### Other Directories
- `module/` - Feature modules and business logic components
- `ui/` - React components and UI elements
- `utility/` - Helper functions and utilities

## Key Features
- Uses React 19 with TypeScript
- Implements a repository pattern (e.g., PaneRepository)
- Modular architecture with clear separation of concerns
- Styled with CSS/SASS
- Uses Vite for fast development and building

## Development Scripts
- `yarn dev` - Start development server
- `yarn build` - Build for production
- `yarn preview` - Preview production build
- `yarn lint:check` - Check for linting issues
- `yarn lint:fix` - Fix linting issues
- `yarn format:fix` - Format code with Prettier

## Dependencies
- Core: React, React DOM
- UI: @enun/react, @radix-ui/colors
- State Management: @enun/store
- Utilities: lodash.debounce, nanoid
- Development: TypeScript, Vite, SASS
